{"images":[],"manifest":{"budgetTokens":15000,"countMethod":"proxy","model":"gpt-6-luna","packSha":"5f9ab703af7c13aec0d6e9fe46e2323a0e9c4b40350531d6ba162aaac55c8882","packTokens":3026,"recipeVersion":"1","redactions":0,"sections":[{"id":"platform","tokens":215,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"tpl","tokens":51,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"spans","tokens":1,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"answers","tokens":634,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"sentences","tokens":2071,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"task","tokens":6,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"}],"stage":"round-trip"},"pointers":[],"system":"PLATFORM. This product is designed and built as a web app, and nothing else. Where the requirements ask for a mobile app, a phone app, an iOS or Android app, treat them as the same features in one responsive web app that works well on a phone's browser: never stop, park, ask or leave a requirement out because it names a mobile app, and never plan a native app, an app store step or a phone-only frame. Every page is responsive: it is laid out for a phone, a tablet and a desktop width, with touch-sized controls on the narrow one. What only a native app can do (push notifications, background location, a home-screen icon) is given its closest web form (an in-app notice or email, the browser's location prompt, an installable web app) and said so.\n\nMap each restated sentence to the original intent spans (I-n) and answers (Q-n) it comes from. A sentence that matches none gets empty lists. Every sentence n must appear once.","tools":[],"user":"<artifact id=\"spans\" kind=\"intent\" sha=\"\">\n[]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"answers\" kind=\"answers\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-1\",\n  \"question\": \"How should users authenticate to the driver, staff, and customer areas?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Use individual email-and-password accounts with self-service password reset.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-2\",\n  \"question\": \"Who can create, deactivate, and assign roles and access scopes to users, including a staff member’s warehouses and a customer user’s organisation?\",\n  \"answer\": \"A System Administrator manages accounts, roles, warehouse access, and customer-organisation access.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-3\",\n  \"question\": \"For a customer’s recall response, may reported on-hand, used/dispensed, and destroyed quantities total less than the quantity delivered, leaving a remainder unaccounted?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Allow a smaller total; track the remainder as unaccounted until it is later accounted for or written off with a signed justification.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-4\",\n  \"question\": \"How long must the handover signature and delivery photo remain available?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Retain them for seven years, matching the audit-record retention period.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-5\",\n  \"question\": \"What existing records, if any, must be brought into the new system at launch so lot tracing and recall quantities work from the start?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Start with no imported records; enter opening lots and stock in the new app.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-6\",\n  \"question\": \"Who is authorized to sign a write-off of unaccounted recall quantities?\",\n  \"answer\": \"A Quality Manager.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-7\",\n  \"question\": \"For a partial refusal, can the receiver refuse a quantity within a shipper box, or only accept/refuse whole boxes?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Record acceptance or refusal only for whole boxes, with a reason for each refused box.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-8\",\n  \"question\": \"What tier limits, allowance budgets, and permitted temperature ranges should drive excursion recommendations, and are they shared or product-specific?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Use one configured set of tier limits and allowances for all products.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"sentences\" kind=\"restated\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"n\": 1,\n  \"text\": \"Build Meridian as a responsive web app with individual email-and-password sign-in and password reset for driver, staff, and customer areas.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 2,\n  \"text\": \"Provide System Administrator screens to create and deactivate accounts and assign roles, staff warehouse access, and customer-organisation access.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 3,\n  \"text\": \"Show drivers only their assigned routes for today, with stops in route order.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 4,\n  \"text\": \"Compare scanned shipper boxes with expected boxes before departure, report missing and wrong-route boxes, and block departure until all expected boxes are scanned and wrong-route boxes are removed or corrected.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 5,\n  \"text\": \"Show dispatchers each route stop’s status and last-updated time.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 6,\n  \"text\": \"Show each route box’s latest available temperature, status, and alerts from gateway data, and mark cached temperature data as stale while disconnected.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 7,\n  \"text\": \"For boxes on hold, display “Do not deliver” and the returned hold reason, and prevent their handover while permitting handover of deliverable boxes.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 8,\n  \"text\": \"When online, display “Do not deliver” and prevent handover of any scanned box reported as recalled.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 9,\n  \"text\": \"Let drivers record eligible handovers with receiver name, signature, delivery photo, actual handover time, and available browser location.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 10,\n  \"text\": \"If browser location is denied or unavailable, allow an otherwise eligible handover and record location as unavailable.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 11,\n  \"text\": \"Let drivers record full or partial refusals only by whole box and require a reason for each refused box; show returned refusal and quarantine statuses.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 12,\n  \"text\": \"While offline, retain loading, handover, and refusal work locally across session expiry or sign-out; after connectivity returns, send queued work automatically, requiring re-authentication if needed, preserving handover occurrence time, and reusing the same handover identifier on retries.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 13,\n  \"text\": \"When an assigned route changes while a driver is offline, show route differences, require review and resolution of affected unsent work before continuing, and preserve completed offline handovers.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 14,\n  \"text\": \"When an offline handover conflicts with a hold or recall upon synchronization, retain and flag the handover and display the returned quality-case result.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 15,\n  \"text\": \"Show Quality reviewers the full excursion temperature history, allowance used and remaining for each tier, and returned recommendation, using configured tier rules and values.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 16,\n  \"text\": \"Provide a single-person quality-decision flow only for an excursion within the first tier above or below the permitted band with allowance remaining; otherwise require a Quality Officer proposal and separate approval by a different Quality Manager, with written justification when a decision opposes the recommendation.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 17,\n  \"text\": \"Require identity confirmation using the account’s sign-in method and a reason when a user signs a quality decision; show signed decisions as read-only with a separate superseding-decision action and display both earlier and superseding signed records in history.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 18,\n  \"text\": \"When the service returns a quality disposition, show resulting stock, order, and route status and earlier and current dispositions when superseded; show errors and unchanged statuses when a superseding disposition is rejected.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 19,\n  \"text\": \"Collect destruction date, quantity, and witness for rejected stock, and prevent entry of a quantity greater than the displayed rejected quantity.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 20,\n  \"text\": \"Identify decisions waiting more than four hours as escalated in the Quality Manager’s waiting-decisions view.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 21,\n  \"text\": \"Provide eligible Quality Managers a flow to start and close recalls with signed actions; recall start collects product, one or more lots, reason, and severity, and the screen displays each returned result.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 22,\n  \"text\": \"Display the returned recall trace, including warehouse locations, boxes, routes, customer deliveries, quantities, delivery dates, receivers, and the trace total alongside received quantity when supplied.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 23,\n  \"text\": \"Show customers recall notices in the portal, link them to affected deliveries, and provide a response entry point.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 24,\n  \"text\": \"Let customers submit per-delivery on-hand, used or dispensed, and destroyed quantities; allow totals below the delivered amount as unaccounted and reject totals above it.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 25,\n  \"text\": \"Show recall progress as the returned percentage accounted for, outstanding customers, and reminder status when supplied; let a Quality Manager submit a signed write-off justification for unaccounted quantity and block recall closure while unaccounted quantity lacks a signed write-off.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 26,\n  \"text\": \"Show customers only their organisation’s current and past orders, allocated lots and expiry dates, order status, and in-transit delivery arrival and temperature status, without exposing other route customers.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 27,\n  \"text\": \"Provide a PDF certificate for each completed delivery containing products, lots, expiry dates, quantities, receiver, handover time, each box’s temperature chart from sealing to handover, excursions, and signed excursion decisions.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 28,\n  \"text\": \"When late readings produce a new certificate version, list new and earlier versions and keep each available for download.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 29,\n  \"text\": \"Present the customer portal and certificates in the user’s selected English or Arabic; render Arabic right to left, including tables and charts, and show dates and times in the account’s configured time zone.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 30,\n  \"text\": \"Provide an audit-trail screen showing returned entries with actor, time, changed fields, old and new values, and supplied reason; support filters by record, user, date range, and action type and export of the filtered view.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 31,\n  \"text\": \"Show the returned history of a lot from receipt through delivery or destruction in time order.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 32,\n  \"text\": \"Provide on-screen reports for selected date ranges and warehouses, with CSV export of displayed figures, including specified excursion, refusal/destruction, delivery, decision-time, expiry, and recall measures; limit warehouse choices to the staff user’s access scope.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 33,\n  \"text\": \"Provide forms for authorized staff to enter opening lots and stock records and submit them to the service.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 34,\n  \"text\": \"Make recorded handover signatures and delivery photos available from a delivery record within its seven-year evidence-retention period.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 35,\n  \"text\": \"Support the latest two browser versions of Chrome, Edge, Safari, and Firefox; make the main flows conform to WCAG 2.1 AA; render the full recall trace returned for the assumed launch scale; and support the assumed first-year product scale and requested lot-trace screen response time.\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\nMap the sentences."}